---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
import { affiliates } from '../../data/affiliates';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Best AI Writing Tools for Small Marketing Teams (Under $100/mo)"
  description="Research-based picks for AI writing tools that can fit a small marketing team budget under $100/month as of August 2026."
  moneyPage
>
  <AffiliateDisclosure />
  <article class="prose-spl mt-6 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">August 4, 2026 · Research comparison</p>
    <h1 class="!mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">Best AI Writing Tools for Small Marketing Teams (Under $100/mo)</h1>
    <p>
      Small marketing teams rarely need an enterprise content suite on day one. This guide maps AI writing options that
      commonly fit a <strong>combined team spend under about $100/month</strong> (as of August 2026—vendor tiers change;
      verify live pricing). We focus on workflow fit, not hype claims or fabricated long-term trials. AI-assisted drafting
      helped organize this research; judgments are editorial.
    </p>

    <h2>What “under $100/mo” should mean</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One shared seat (or a small-seat plan) that covers drafting for 1–3 marketers</li>
      <li>Enough monthly words/documents for weekly blogs, emails, and landing copy—not unlimited agency volume</li>
      <li>Optional light SEO help if it stays inside the budget band</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you need brand kits for 10 writers, multi-brand workspaces, or a full SEO research suite, you will usually break
      $100 fast—and that can still be the right call. This article is for teams trying <em>not</em> to.
    </p>

    <h2>Writesonic — budget draft + SEO bundling</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={affiliates.writesonic.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Writesonic</a>
      is often positioned as a lower-cost writer with article/SEO features in the same product. For a two-person content
      duo that drafts and lightly optimizes in one place, that consolidation can keep spend inside the band better than
      paying for a premium writer <em>plus</em> a separate optimizer.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Best for:</strong> frequent publishers who want generation and light SEO together.
      <strong>Skip if:</strong> you need deep brand governance or best-in-class SERP scoring.
    </p>

    <h2>Frase — briefs and optimize without a heavy suite</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={affiliates.frase.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Frase</a>
      is a practical pick when the bottleneck is SERP-informed briefs and coverage—not campaign template libraries.
      Entry plans have historically sat in a small-team-friendly range; confirm current document limits against how many
      posts you ship per month.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Best for:</strong> SEO-led teams that live in outlines and topic coverage.
      <strong>Skip if:</strong> you mainly need ad/social campaign copy with brand controls.
    </p>

    <h2>Copy.ai — only if workflows earn the seat</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={affiliates.copyai.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Copy.ai</a>
      can fit a lean budget when you actually use workflow automation (research → draft → reuse for outbound or GTM).
      If your team only opens a chat box twice a week, you are paying for machinery you will not use—pick a simpler writer
      instead. (Copy.ai’s affiliate program availability changes; we still cover it editorially.)
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Best for:</strong> GTM-minded marketers automating repeatable writing steps.
      <strong>Skip if:</strong> you want a pure long-form editor or hate configuring workflows.
    </p>

    <h2>Jasper — usually above this band for “real” team use</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={affiliates.jasper.url} rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Jasper</a>
      is strong for brand voice and marketing workflows, but meaningful team plans often sit above a strict $100/mo
      ceiling once you add seats and brand features. Treat Jasper as the upgrade path when brand governance becomes the
      bottleneck—not the default under-$100 pick. (Jasper affiliate access is often invite-only; coverage here is editorial.)
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Best for:</strong> brand-led teams ready to pay for structure.
      <strong>Skip if:</strong> the hard constraint is staying under ~$100/mo all-in.
    </p>

    <h2>Also consider (non-affiliate stack reality)</h2>
    <p>
      General assistants (ChatGPT, Claude, etc.) plus a human editor remain a legitimate under-$100 stack for many
      startups. You trade structured SEO scoring and marketing templates for flexibility. Pair with a cheap optimizer
      later only if drafts consistently miss SERP coverage.
    </p>

    <h2>Practical pick under $100</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>SEO articles are the job → Frase (or Writesonic if you also need heavy generation).</li>
      <li>Mixed marketing drafts + light SEO → Writesonic.</li>
      <li>Repeatable GTM/outbound content steps → Copy.ai, if you will run workflows weekly.</li>
      <li>Brand kit / multi-channel campaigns outgrow the band → revisit Jasper (and accept higher spend).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Side-by-side Best for / Skip if:
      <a href="/compare/ai-writing-tools-under-100">Under $100 AI writing comparison</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
